<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN BACOB INTERESTED IN AUSTRIAN CREDITANSTALT.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN BACOB INTERESTED IN AUSTRIAN CREDITANSTALT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bacob, one of Belgium's top-seven banks is &quot;interested&quot; in Austrian bank Creditanstalt, Bacob said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It is true that we are interested, but it is not correct that we would be involved in a bid for Creditantstalt,&quot; a Bacob spokesman told Reuters.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, an Austrian newspaper reported that Bacob was in talks with Die Erste Oesterreichische SparCasse Bank (First Austrian) in a new bid for Creditanstalt-Bankverein.  </p>
<p>The Bacob spokesman declined further comment.</p>
<p>Austrian savings bank First Austrian announced on Tuesday it planned to form a consortium to bid for Creditanstalt, which is currently being privatised.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6813, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
